Package: dev.airdevs.dsh
Name: DSH CLI (DeepSeek Harness)
Version: 0.2.1-rc.5+ios15
Section: Terminal Support
Priority: optional
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Air-Devs <air2@localhost>
Description: DeepSeek Harness CLI for rootless jailbroken iOS (A11 compatible)
 Bundles Node.js 22.12.0 (pure arm64, standard MAP_JIT, tested on iPhone X)
 plus a pure-JS dsh 0.2.1-rc.5 tree (no native addons) patched for Node 22.12.
 +ios3 auto-detects a SIGBUS-free V8 tier at first launch and falls back to
 a zero-JIT (--jitless) HTTP shim on A11 / iOS 16 rootless. Type `dsh` to boot.
 +ios4 adds a Safari 16.7 (iOS 16 / WebKit 16.6) browser polyfill for the web
 frontend: AbortSignal.any, Promise.withResolvers, Object.groupBy, Map.groupBy,
 Array.fromAsync (all Safari 17.4+). Also silences the harmless V8
 --expose_wasm warning in the zero-JIT tier.
 +ios5 fixes "directoryPicker/list failed: Load failed" in the web workspace:
 the zero-JIT fetch shim no longer overrides the native Headers / Request /
 Response / FormData globals (the backend web framework needs them to build
 HTTP responses); it overrides only fetch and WebSocket. One-file hotfix:
 sh fix-api-load-failed.sh, then restart dsh. New installs need no action.
 +ios6 fixes "DeepSeek Messages transport failed" (TRANSPORT) when sending a
 chat message: the zero-JIT ShimResponse.body getter was not idempotent, while
 the DeepSeek SSE path reads response.body twice; the second read threw
 "Body is unusable" and was folded into a TRANSPORT error on every retry.
 Also adds formData()/bytes(). One-file hotfix: sh fix-transport.sh, restart dsh.
 +ios7 preinstalls the official @tencent-connect/dsh-qqbot 0.5.5 plugin:
 its pure-JS dependency tree is bundled into node_modules (no .node addons),
 peer packages reuse the host 0.2.1-rc.5 tree, and first launch appends one
 plugin row to $DSH_HOME/cordis.patch.yml. `dsh plugin add` always exits 127
 on a phone because dsh forwards to pnpm, which is not on the device -- this
 build removes that requirement entirely. Set QQBOT_APPID / QQBOT_SECRET in
 /var/jb/etc/dsh/qqbot.env, or leave them empty to scan a QR code at startup.
 DSH_QQBOT=0 dsh disables the plugin temporarily. Hotfix for older installs:
 sh install-qqbot.sh (no need to re-transfer the 113MB deb), then restart dsh.
 +ios8 fixes "previous conversation disappears after restarting dsh". The
 Node 22.12 zlib fallback made session-persistence-jsonl WRITE gzip frames
 while its reader still demanded ZSTD_MAGIC, so sessions were written but
 never readable. Default compression is now "none" (plain JSONL), self-
 consistent on Node 22.12. New installs are fixed at build time; upgraded
 devices get an automatic one-shot migration by postinst (existing gzip
 session logs are decompressed and the originals archived under
 $DSH_HOME/sessions-legacy-zstd/). Manual hotfix: sh fix-session.sh,
 then restart dsh. Plain JSONL is not interoperable with desktop zstd logs.
 +ios9 preinstalls @xmanrui/dsh-im 5.10.0 (10 IM channels: Feishu,
 WeChat, WeCom, DingTalk, QQ, Slack, Telegram, Discord, WhatsApp, Matrix).
 Its 114 runtime deps are bundled in a private nested node_modules (1275
 files / 0 native addons), isolated from the host and the +ios7 QQ Bot tree.
 Node >=22.19 is NOT required: the plugin runs on the bundled Node 22.12.0
 after a build-time zero-JIT patch (A11 nowasm has no WebAssembly; the
 bundled libsignal WASM glue otherwise aborts the whole plugin import).
 First launch registers the plugin in $DSH_HOME/cordis.patch.yml and creates
 the profile->package ESM resolution link. DSH_IM=0 dsh disables it.
 Hotfix for older installs: sh install-im.sh (7.8MB, self-contained), then
 restart dsh; --status / --remove supported. WhatsApp encrypted history-sync
 hash is the only degraded capability on the zero-JIT tier.
 +ios10 fixes the last A11 failure: "1 extraneous did not activate:
 xmanrui-dsh-im: failed to import: ERR_UNKNOWN_BUILTIN_MODULE: No such
 built-in module: node:sqlite". dsh-im 5.10.0 has a top-level static ESM
 import of node:sqlite; the bundled Node 22.12.0 gates that builtin behind
 --experimental-sqlite (22.13+ enables it by default, which is why a build
 host could not reproduce it). All dsh launch paths now pass the flag, so
 the plugin's SQLite cache works with zero degradation. dsh-doctor gains a
 check that really loads node:sqlite plus an idempotent im-qqbot auto-mount
 (removes the stale WARN on devices that ran install-im.sh before dsh).
 Hotfix for +ios9 devices: sh fix-sqlite.sh (no 125MB re-transfer needed).
 +ios11 fixes two false-green issues reported after +ios10. (1) The
 home-level cordis.patch.yml was created by an earlier hotfix running as
 root, so the mobile user got "cannot create ...: Permission denied" on
 line 45 of the dsh wrapper while the wrapper still printed "plugin
 mounted" because the append error was swallowed. dsh, dsh-doctor and
 the hotfix now use write-temp-then-atomic-replace, which also repairs
 file ownership, and report a warning instead of faking success. (2) A
 leftover pnpm-layout copy at node_modules/.pnpm/@xmanrui+dsh-im/5.10.0/
 was the copy actually imported by the ESM resolver; it never received
 the +ios9 zero-JIT patch, so dsh-im failed with "ge.lthashantitampering_new
 is not a function" even though dsh-doctor's single-file check passed.
 The hotfix scans every @xmanrui/dsh-im/lib/index.js on the device and
 patches each one; dsh-doctor gains check 19 that fails if any copy is
 unpatched. Hotfix: sh fix-ios11.sh (also written as fix-sqlite.sh).
 +ios12 is a clean-base release: the two previously bundled plugins
 (@xmanrui/dsh-im and @tencent-connect/dsh-qqbot) are removed from the
 package entirely, and the wrapper no longer writes cordis.patch.yml,
 creates symlinks, or changes ownership. Instead pnpm 10.28.2 (pure JS,
 no native addons) is bundled so the official `dsh plugin --profile web
 add <pkg>` command works on-device instead of exiting 127. Run
 dsh-compat after installing dsh-im to apply the A11 zero-JIT patch to
 every local copy. Fixes the "cannot create new session" EACCES failure:
 dsh-home-heal.cjs uses rename(2) to repair root-owned sessions/ trees
 and profile config files without needing root, migrating historical
 *.jsonl sessions. All earlier fixes (tier probe, fetch-shim, Safari 16
 polyfill, session compression=none, --experimental-sqlite) are retained.
 +ios13 fixes two regressions found on a real iPhone X after +ios12.
 (1) "dsh: fatal uncaught exception -> patches: patches.yml/cordis.patch.yml
 must be a top-level YAML array of loader patch entries". The +ios12 heal
 deleted the two bundled-plugin rows and left a comment-only file; js-yaml
 returns null and dsh-app-boot parsePatchList throws on boot. It also
 cleaned only the home-level file, leaving profiles/*/cordis.patch.yml
 rows referencing the now-unbundled plugins (headless ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND).
 dsh-home-heal.cjs now scans both levels, removes whole blocks, and
 forces a valid top-level YAML array ([] when empty); it repairs devices
 already broken by +ios12. dsh-doctor runs heal before its checks and
 truly parses every patch file. (2) "dsh plugin ... pnpm was not found"
 (127): package exports split the CLI (lib/types/operations.js) and the
 web service (lib/index.js) into two artifacts; both spawn pnpm via execa
 with extendEnv:false and a dsh-built env, so on-device PATH/shebang
 lookup fails. apply_pnpm_abs_patch.cjs injects an absolute bundled-node
 command plus the absolute pure-JS pnpm.cjs path into all 5+5 call sites
 in each artifact, bypassing PATH entirely. Both fixes ship in the deb
 and in the one-shot sh fix-ios13.sh hotfix (no 125MB re-transfer).
 +ios14 fixes two more failures seen on a real iPhone X after
 +ios13. (1) "Command was killed with SIGBUS" when removing a
 plugin: the absolute-path pnpm launcher added in +ios13 lost
 the V8 tier flags, so the 7.2MB pnpm bundle compiled JIT/WASM
 on a background thread and hit A11 pthread_jit_write_protect.
 Both CLI and service artifacts now inject the zero-JIT tier
 (--jitless --no-expose-wasm --require fetch-shim.cjs); devices
 already on +ios13 are upgraded in place, not skipped. The pnpm
 wrapper and the hotfix pnpm calls carry the same flags.
 (2) "failed to create session: EACCES ... session.v4.jsonl":
 heal bailed out on the first line when $DSH_HOME itself was
 root-owned, and treeWritable checked only directories so a
 root 444 session file was missed; dsh-doctor only probed the
 sessions top level. heal now repairs $DSH_HOME ownership by
 chmod/rename-swap, checks files too, fixes each unwritable
 *.jsonl, and transfers root-owned trees to mobile when run as
 root. dsh-doctor check 20 really creates a deep session file.
 All fixes ship in sh fix-ios14.sh (no 125MB re-transfer).
 +ios15 fixes the Web UI plugin install page and the plugin market on a
 real iPhone X. (1) "All manual install methods in the Install Plugin
 dialog fail, while AI-assisted install succeeds": the service artifact
 checkGithubConnection() spawned a bare `git ls-remote` for git/GitHub
 specs; iOS has no git binary, so the optional reachability probe died
 with ENOENT and aborted installBundle. AI-assisted install rewrites the
 repo address to an npm name/tarball and never hits the probe. +ios15
 short-circuits that optional probe (pnpm downloads via codeload HTTP).
 (2) "Plugin Market fails to load with a pile of errors": fetchIndex used
 redirect:"error" so any CDN/http->https redirect threw, and
 parseIndexInWorker spawned a Worker with execArgv:[] which re-enabled
 V8 JIT on a background thread -> SIGBUS on A11 in the zero-JIT tier.
 +ios15 switches to redirect:"follow" and parses the index on the main
 thread via a byte-identical derivative of the official worker.cjs.
 (3) Web UI manual install now transforms ecosystem-plugin specs before
 submit: GitHub/git addresses become pnpm hosted-git shorthands, and
 iOS/Safari-incompatible plugins (native addons, Electron, Playwright,
 Node>=24) get a clear hint + alternative (never hard-blocked). This
 transform is injected ONLY into the Web UI manual-install client.js;
 the AI tool (tools.js) and CLI (operations.js) are untouched, so
 AI-assisted install never applies it. GitHub /tree/<branch> refs
 containing slashes (e.g. tree/release/v2) are handled; 32 spec
 transform cases are regression-tested. Safari 16.6 polyfill extended
 with Promise.try/RegExp.escape/toSorted/Uint8Array base64-hex/etc.
 All fixes ship in sh fix-ios15.sh (no 125MB re-transfer); dsh-doctor
 gains checks 23-26. Build is byte-reproducible: sh bootstrap.sh pulls
 the two >100MB assets from Releases with SHA-256 checks, then sh
 build.sh fixes mtimes and uses SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH; verify-repro.sh
 proves two builds are identical and verify-deb.sh independently
 un-packs the shipped .deb and asserts all 57 landing conditions.
 Version upgrade deliberately deferred: no iOS arm64 Node >=24.9.0
 that is as reliable as the bundled 22.12.0 exists (see
 docs/DSH-NODE-UPGRADE-EVALUATION.md); stays on dsh 0.2.1-rc.5.
Homepage: https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
